2 container (/var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img) unlocked via a root-only keyfile (/etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/srv-secure.key), mapped to /dev/mapper/secure_srv and formatted ext4, mounted at /srv/secure. Configured /etc/crypttab (noauto luks entry) and /etc/fstab (with x-systemd.requires= on the cryptsetup service) so systemd's generated mount unit automatically pulls in decryption and mounts /srv/secure at every boot without any interactive input. Verified end-to-end: rebooted node1 via `systemctl reboot`, confirmed boot_id changed (proving an actual restart, not just a service bounce), and confirmed /srv/secure was auto-mounted post-boot with the pre-restart test file's SHA-256 checksum unchanged.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS/disk layout (AlmaLinux 9.6, single vda disk, no spare block device)\",\"Installed cryptsetup package\",\"Created 1G backing file /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img and 4096-byte random keyfile /etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/srv-secure.key (mode 600)\",\"Ran cryptsetup luksFormat (LUKS2) on the backing file using the keyfile\",\"Opened the LUKS container as /dev/mapper/secure_srv, formatted ext4, mounted at /srv/secure\",\"Added crypttab entry (secure_srv <img> <keyfile> luks,noauto) and fstab entry (with x-systemd.requires=systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service) for auto-unlock and auto-mount at boot\",\"Verified the systemd-generated srv-secure.mount unit correctly pulls in the cryptsetup service when started, confirming boot-time dependency wiring\",\"Wrote a healthcheck test file with a captured SHA-256 checksum, and captured pre-restart boot_id baseline\",\"Triggered systemctl reboot on node1, polled until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed new boot_id (proving actual restart) and verified /srv/secure was automatically unlocked and mounted with no manual steps, with the healthcheck file's checksum unchanged\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline: encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure with data present pre-restart, and boot identity captured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d32b044bf9ae40b2\",\"cmd-393794349bf84f6e\",\"cmd-802a29a2b9054d5c\"],\"summary\":\"/srv/secure mounted from /dev/mapper/secure_srv (LUKS-backed), healthcheck.txt written with known SHA-256, pre-restart boot_id=31b01b46-96de-4ded-a021-49887e7d4053 captured\"},{\"requirement\":\"Auto-unlock/auto-mount configuration in place (crypttab + fstab with systemd dependency) validated before reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c09fba7f07a94d83\",\"cmd-393794349bf84f6e\"],\"summary\":\"crypttab (noauto luks entry) and fstab (x-systemd.requires=systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service) entries added; manually starting srv-secure.mount unit correctly triggered the cryptsetup dependency and mounted the volume, proving the wiring works\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-35b0cf4bad6342a5\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued via backgrounded/delayed subshell so the exec call returned REBOOT_TRIGGERED before the node went down\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart confirmed unreachable then reachable again, with changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6371a8367bda4a62\",\"cmd-3ebecaf13fdb4a5c\"],\"summary\":\"Immediately after reboot trigger, exec timed out (node down); subsequent poll succeeded with new boot_id=b22cc786-326c-4cfa-826e-133f121ad6ec (differs from baseline) and new uptime-since timestamp\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery: encrypted volume auto-unlocked, mounted, and data intact without manual intervention\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1de2f83584e14bd5\"],\"summary\":\"Post-boot, systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service and srv-secure.mount both show Active since the boot time (auto-started, no manual commands run), /srv/secure is mounted from /dev/mapper/secure_srv, and healthcheck.txt SHA-256 matches the pre-restart baseline exactly\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created an encrypted volume on node1 (AlmaLinux 9) using a 1GB file-backed LUKS2 container (/var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img) unlocked via a root-only keyfile (/etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/srv-secure.key), mapped to /dev/mapper/secure_srv and formatted ext4, mounted at /srv/secure. Configured /etc/crypttab (noauto luks entry) and /etc/fstab (with x-systemd.requires= on the cryptsetup service) so systemd's generated mount unit automatically pulls in decryption and mounts /srv/secure at every boot without any interactive input. Verified end-to-end: rebooted node1 via `systemctl reboot`, confirmed boot_id changed (proving an actual restart, not just a service bounce), and confirmed /srv/secure was auto-mounted post-boot with the pre-restart test file's SHA-256 checksum unchanged.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS/disk layout (AlmaLinux 9.6, single vda disk, no spare block device)","Installed cryptsetup package","Created 1G backing file /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img and 4096-byte random keyfile /etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/srv-secure.key (mode 600)","Ran cryptsetup luksFormat (LUKS2) on the backing file using the keyfile","Opened the LUKS container as /dev/mapper/secure_srv, formatted ext4, mounted at /srv/secure","Added crypttab entry (secure_srv <img> <keyfile> luks,noauto) and fstab entry (with x-systemd.requires=systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service) for auto-unlock and auto-mount at boot","Verified the systemd-generated srv-secure.mount unit correctly pulls in the cryptsetup service when started, confirming boot-time dependency wiring","Wrote a healthcheck test file with a captured SHA-256 checksum, and captured pre-restart boot_id baseline","Triggered systemctl reboot on node1, polled until exec access returned","Confirmed new boot_id (proving actual restart) and verified /srv/secure was automatically unlocked and mounted with no manual steps, with the healthcheck file's checksum unchanged"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Healthy baseline: encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure with data present pre-restart, and boot identity captured","command_ids":["cmd-d32b044bf9ae40b2","cmd-393794349bf84f6e","cmd-802a29a2b9054d5c"],"summary":"/srv/secure mounted from /dev/mapper/secure_srv (LUKS-backed), healthcheck.txt written with known SHA-256, pre-restart boot_id=31b01b46-96de-4ded-a021-49887e7d4053 captured"},{"requirement":"Auto-unlock/auto-mount configuration in place (crypttab + fstab with systemd dependency) validated before reboot","command_ids":["cmd-c09fba7f07a94d83","cmd-393794349bf84f6e"],"summary":"crypttab (noauto luks entry) and fstab (x-systemd.requires=systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service) entries added; manually starting srv-secure.mount unit correctly triggered the cryptsetup dependency and mounted the volume, proving the wiring works"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-35b0cf4bad6342a5"],"summary":"systemctl reboot issued via backgrounded/delayed subshell so the exec call returned REBOOT_TRIGGERED before the node went down"},{"requirement":"Node restart confirmed unreachable then reachable again, with changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-6371a8367bda4a62","cmd-3ebecaf13fdb4a5c"],"summary":"Immediately after reboot trigger, exec timed out (node down); subsequent poll succeeded with new boot_id=b22cc786-326c-4cfa-826e-133f121ad6ec (differs from baseline) and new uptime-since timestamp"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery: encrypted volume auto-unlocked, mounted, and data intact without manual intervention","command_ids":["cmd-1de2f83584e14bd5"],"summary":"Post-boot, systemd-cryptsetup@secure_srv.service and srv-secure.mount both show Active since the boot time (auto-started, no manual commands run), /srv/secure is mounted from /dev/mapper/secure_srv, and healthcheck.txt SHA-256 matches the pre-restart baseline exactly"}]},"ttft_ms":2203,"type":"result","duration_ms":108698,"uuid":"ee7ba560-d4c2-4020-80d2-c103d96314bf","ttft_stream_ms":1404,"time_to_request_ms":87,"first_content_frame_ms":1783,"queued_turn_count":0}
